WEBVTT

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.360
"Kodomo no Odocha"

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.700
That rumor that I love you

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.330
is true, yes it is.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.830
You can't ignore it either.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.420
Whether you're awake or asleep,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.050
please don't be embarrassed.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.640
Is it a sin if I sneak into your heart

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.310
by ridding you...

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.480
...of your other love?

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.060
At sunset,

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.570
when the children go home,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.530
Today's incident is burning love!

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:58.410
You can tell it accurately.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.490
7 O'Clock News!

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:04.290
Please, our relationship...

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:09.960
Please don't blame it on the true kiss

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.840
In a city without light,

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.680
let's burn the fire of love.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.100
Don't be so easy going

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.350
The existence is a mistake

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.850
You're asking for something not there.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:33.280
I'm Kurata Sana,

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:36.700
a 6th grader and TV personality
affiliated with Gekidan Komawari.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:39.870
My beloved Mama is a famous novelist,
who has even won the Aoki Laureate Prize.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.870
The chipmunk on her head
is Maro-chan.

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:43.620
My former boyfriend,
Sagami Rei-kun.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:47.210
Right now, he's earnestly on the way
to becoming a fine manager.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:49.210
The mysterious white bat
straight man, Babbit.

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:51.040
I love peeled bananas!

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.090
Hayama Akito,
my natural enemy.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:57.220
Even so, right now, when I'm around him,
I'm relaxed for some reason.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:01.470
The handsome and gifted child actor
and trumpeter, Naozumi-kun.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:05.810
Good morning!!

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:08.480
G- good morning,
Sana-chan.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.810
You sure are cheery
in the morning.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.480
That's no fair, Hayama!
How come you're the only one unharmed?

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.480
I'm not.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:14.480
Oh, I see...

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:19.490
Hey, listen, listen! I, Kurata Sana,
might be putting out a book, of all things!

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:23.330
"Honto~?" ("Really?")

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.830
Are you guys
trying to make a pun?

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.620
"Hon to~?" ("A book?")

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.500
What kind of book?

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.830
Oh, about how in life, what lies
one sun ahead is a 5-sun nail.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:30.500
Five sun is about this long.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.630
"15.15 cm"

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.590
Remember, when we went
to outdoor school,

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:35.840
I had to write an essay on remorse,
together with Hayama?

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.840
Yeah, from when
you two went missing.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.340
Right, right.
Mama's editor, Onda-san,

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:44.510
--saw my composition from then, and...
--Sana-chan, that's so interesting!
Would you right more? Let's put out a book!

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.020
--We'll get the royalties!
--Let's put out a book!
Let's put out a book!

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.190
So, you're turning your
composition into a book?

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:50.520
Call it an "essay," please!

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.850
Essay?

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.520
Essay?
Essay?

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.530
♪ Essay, "dossei,"
fur seal, ♪

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.530
♪ Write, write, round, round,
triangle, square! ♪

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:59.530
♪ I can't write! I can't write!
I can't write a thing! ♪

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:02.160
♪ The next-door fence is a persimmon
that often eats guests! ♪

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.450
Sana-chan sure does have the accelerator
to the floor today. Go, go!

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.120
Must be hard
playing the lead role.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:09.500
Then, it could be interesting
if you wrote about this upcoming party, huh?

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.170
Oh, speaking of the party, ma'am,

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:16.130
I invited Kamura Naozumi-kun
to the party, too.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:17.840
Naozumi-kun?

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.510
--Did you hear that, Akito-kun?
Kamura Naozumi is coming to the party.
--All right!
Yay, Sana-chan!

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:20.510
--Did you hear that, Akito-kun?
Kamura Naozumi is coming to the party.
--I'm still not yet completely sure
he's coming, though.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:21.510
--Doesn't matter.
--I'm still not yet completely sure
he's coming, though.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:22.840
--But he likes Sana-chan.
--I'm still not yet completely sure
he's coming, though.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:24.850
I told you,
it doesn't matter.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.140
Hey, Hayama!

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.810
Have you bought a middle
birthday present for me yet?

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.020
--No, not yet.
--Now, see here!

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:35.190
--Don't forget to buy it! You're not
getting away with coming empty-handed.
--You're hurting me, Sana-chan!

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:38.150
Oh, I'll go. I'll go as the
empty-empty handed-handed alien.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.190
--What's that?
--You'll do what!?

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:43.870
--Don't kid around! Don't let me down!
Don't feel around! Buy it! Buy it!
Buy me a present! Buy it!
--The bura-bura alien is here.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.950
--Yay! Naozumi-kun
is coming, coming, coming!
--Empty-empty handed-handed, here he is.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:50.200
--Um, it's about time we started class.
--The bura-bura alien is here.
Empty-empty handed-handed, here he is.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.880
"A Heart-pounding Kiss at Christmas"

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:01.470
Actually, you were going to buy
your present along time ago.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:04.140
Then Kamura Naozumi
suddenly showed up.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:07.140
And what's worse,
now he's coming to the party.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:10.140
What's the matter,
Akito-kun?

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.140
I don't know...

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:13.480
...what kind of present
should I buy her?

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.810
Akito-kun! You don't
have to worry about it!

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:18.150
You'll find something
when we look in the stores!

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.150
Here, how about this place?

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:23.820
This place is full of merchandise
to get a young girl's heart, right?

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.490
You have a hard time dealing
with environments like this, huh?

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.490
H- have I guessed right, Hayama?

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.500
Wow, nice!

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.500
This would look great on Aya-chan,
wouldn't it? Wouldn't it? Wouldn't-

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:35.830
Akito-kun,
have you decided?

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:42.170
Akito-kun, you don't have
to stress so much over this!

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:45.180
Knowing Sana-chan, she's sure to be
thrilled with whatever you get her.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.510
Still, I can't give her
anything with lousy taste.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.850
You show-off.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.520
Akito-kun, could you
hold back today?

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:53.520
No.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.850
Welcome!

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:58.190
What is it
you're looking for?

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:02.440
A Christmas present
for your girlfriend?

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:05.110
How long do you think Akito-kun
can stand to be in this situation?

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.610
About ten more seconds,
I'll bet.

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.290
"RRRRRRR"

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:22.800
Akito-kun!
Wait up!

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.470
--D- do you do that like this?
--No, it's like this.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:26.470
You're good at that, huh?

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:27.800
Akito-kun,
how about this?

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.470
She's already got
one of those.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:32.140
--This? What about this?
--It's not nice to the touch.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.480
"Fish paste"

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.480
This? This would be great!

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.140
Why not just
get her a bouquet?

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.810
How could I buy her flowers?
I'm not Kamura, you know.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:43.480
--To think that Akito-kun
would be this stressed...
--What does she need?

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.150
I know!
A brassiere!

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:49.160
But I don't know her size.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.160
You were serious,
Akito-kun?

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.410
Oh, outside the window!

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:57.160
Sana-chan and Kamura are-!

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.500
You're spilling
your shake again!

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.130
Oh my, he's kissing her...

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:03.460
B- but still, it's just on the cheek,
so it's still safe!

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.800
Thank heavens!
Oh, thank heavens!

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.470
That's a relief, huh?
Huh? Huh? Akito-kun?

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:07.470
Whatever.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.140
Oh, okay.

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:12.140
Still, seeing that big ad,

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:16.480
it feels like she's someone from
a faraway world, and not our friend, huh?

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:19.480
Once she puts out her book,
she'll probably become even more famous.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.810
She's really amazing, huh?

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.480
Never mind that,
Akito-kun, about the present...

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.820
Huh? Oh, yeah...

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:27.490
You don't have to think
so hard about it.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:32.160
Try thinking of something
that made you happy when you got it.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:34.160
It's never happened.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.660
I've never gotten
a present before.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.830
What about that dinosaur?

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:44.840
You told me your father
bought it for you, didn't he?

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:48.670
As I recall, just once,
your father took you someplace-

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:50.510
to that dinosaur exhibit, right?

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.520
Akito...

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.270
If you space off like that,
you're going to get lost.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:05.110
Here.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:11.110
You like dinosaurs, right?

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:12.450
Don't hate them.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.120
Akito?

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.460
Let's throw a party.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:30.800
Your dad can come home early
on Christmas Eve this year.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.140
Father, what is that?

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:37.470
Goods to change me into Santa-san.
I borrowed them from my company.

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:39.480
What company do you
work for, anyway?

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.480
Okay?
Let's throw a party.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.150
I'm going out
on Chirstmas Eve.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:46.820
I have that party
at Kurata's place.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:50.820
Uh, I also have a party,
with my friends.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.490
But I'll be here
on the 25th.

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:55.490
Right! Christmas is really
on the 25th, after all...

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:59.160
All right.
Dad will settle for that.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:00.830
Father has been
strange lately.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.080
You've been strange
since your first appearance.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.130
Christmas... Christmas...
the 25th is Christmas...

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.420
--Natsumi...
--Call me Big Sister!

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:11.090
What is it
that girls want?

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:15.140
Girls!?
You!?

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.430
I get it.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:17.810
Never mind!

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:21.980
Wait, Akito!
Akito!

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:25.150
So long as it's from the heart, she should
be happy with anything you get her.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:30.820
"Anything," she says...
But what, though?

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.780
"The day before the party"

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.780
Rei-kun! We need
one more chair here!

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:35.490
Right!

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:39.160
Isn't this nice? People who find joy
in Christmas are so merry.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:41.500
Nah, I'm not merry!

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.500
Oh, Rei-kun, did you say
you're not "ukare" (merry)?

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:45.790
Check!

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:46.830
What's your favorite animal?

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:48.460
"Uki-uki-uki"
chattering monkeys!

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:49.170
What are you hungry for?

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.500
Ooh, curry!!

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:51.510
What musical instrument
would you like to hear?

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:53.130
--The "ukarere."
--That's "ukulele"!

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:54.800
Right now,
you are...

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:58.180
...in a state of out-of-control,
walking-on-air, ukare merriment!

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:00.640
You think so?

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.600
Myself, on the other hand...

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:06.100
--I'll have to work on Christmas, because
the Sensei won't finish her manuscript.
--Dreams... flowers... love... hope...

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.440
--My girlfriend will tell me
I'm lower than scum.
--Dreams... flowers... love... hope...

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:09.770
Yes, this is Sagami.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:12.440
Ah, Asako?

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:16.110
Huh? Your location shoot is running long?
You won't be home for Christmas Eve?

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:18.450
We won't have our date?

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:21.790
Whoa, Rei-kun suddenly
finds himself in a pinch!

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.450
Here,
Onda-kun!

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:25.120
Oh!
It's finished!

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:27.120
It's not like the others you've been
tricking me with up to now,

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.130
this one is real!

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:30.800
Now I'll be able to take
my girlfriend out and... Yahoo!!

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:31.800
Christmas banzai!
Mayumi!

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.460
What an ironic process to meet.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:37.800
Ironic prospect! It's ironic prospect!
This is processed meat!

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:38.640
Hey!

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:42.810
Oh, Naozumi-kun! You're already here?
You couldn't wait until the party tomorrow?

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:45.810
--No, I'm actually on my way to work...
--Wow, thanks for coming! I've been waiting!

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:50.820
I'm sorry. It turns out that I just
can't make it to your party tomorrow.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:53.150
I really did want
to come, though.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:54.360
I'm sure you did.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:57.150
There's going to be all you can eat,
and a ton of girls are coming.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:01.830
It's not that. It's because this is a party
that you invited me to, Sana-chan.

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:06.500
Well, sure. You wouldn't want to come
to a party that animals invited you to, huh?

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:07.160
Sana-chan...

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.500
Would you figure out
how a boy's heart feels, already!?

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:13.000
I have plans every year
on Christmas Eve.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.340
Plans?
Every year?

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:18.180
My mind was swayed a little
because of your invitation, Sana-chan,

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:20.180
but this thing
I have scheduled is-

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:21.680
Sorry, I have to go.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:27.520
Oh, right! I've got a present
for you on Christmas Eve!

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.020
Be looking forward to it!

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:32.610
A present?

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:36.110
"At that moment,
what was Zenjiro doing?"

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:36.110
Whoa! I came too late!

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:40.870
Kozue-chan? How does Christmas Eve look?
Oh, no good, huh? I see...

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:42.870
This isn't woiking!

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:47.200
I called every goil in the book!
How could I not get a single one!?

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:50.540
What a lonely Christmas
Eve this will be...

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:52.210
W- what's this?

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:54.880
Who is this goil,
with a cute name like Sumire?

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:58.220
Maybe I should
give her a cawl.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:01.140
Hello? Sumire-chan?
My name is Zenjiro.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:04.810
You're probably doing something
on Christmas Eve, so wouldn't be available-

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.470
You're kidding!
You're available!?

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:11.150
Dinnuh? Okay! Okay!
Uh-huh! Okay! I did it!

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:14.650
Thank you, God!

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:19.490
Here's a self-portrait!

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:32.000
Everyone have your glass?

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.340
Okay, let's toast!

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:35.670
But before we do...

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.340
You're going to
break out in song?

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:38.670
Click...

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:43.680
♪ This evening's party
is happy-py-py-py. ♪

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:49.680
♪ Birthday and Christmas,
happy-py-py-py. ♪

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:53.350
Okay, here's to being
doubly happy! Cheers!

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:54.360
Cheers!

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:56.190
Everyone seems to be
enjoying themselves.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:12:00.690
Mother would like to join in,
but- whoa-oa-oa...

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.030
Aren't you trying
too hard to be popular?

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:03.660
Christmas can be tough.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.660
Hayama-san,
congratulations.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:06.990
Not really.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:10.660
I mean, having the middle of Kurata
and your birthdays fall on Christmas Eve,

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:13.330
--you get both merry and happy-
--You talk too much.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:15.670
Yay! Naozumi-kun
is coming, coming, coming!

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:18.000
I don't think
Kamura-kun is coming.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.010
Why not!? Why not!? Why not!?

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:22.340
He said he already has plans every year
on Christmas Eve, that's why.

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:24.010
He can't! He can't! He can't!

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:27.680
Please feel free
to eat this food right up, okay?

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.350
If that's the case, let's drown
our frustration with food!

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:34.690
Oh, no... Aya-chan
likes him that much, too...

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:36.020
Asako...

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:37.520
Rei...

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:40.030
Here's to just
the two of us tonight.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.690
--Whoa, it's cold out here.
Someone let me in.
--"Processed meat," huh?

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:43.360
Happy now?

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:45.700
Hayama...

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:49.370
Here.
Your present.

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:52.370
Go on, take it.
Go on, go on.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:53.710
T- thank you.

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:54.710
Open it!

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:56.710
Go on,
tear it open!

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:05.630
Hey, what's the matter?
Say something.

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:08.260
Hayama, you like dinosaurs, right?

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:12.270
You like dinosaurs, right?

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:15.310
Don't hate them.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:19.650
Oh, I knew it! You have that dinosaur
figure in your room, after all!

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:22.990
If you didn't like them, you wouldn't use
that figure as a decoration.

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:25.320
--Amazing! That's Sana-chan for you!
--I guessed right! Mambo, woo!
Good job! Mambo, cha-cha-cha, woo!

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:27.990
--Actually, when Akito-kun
was little, his father-
--I guessed right! Mambo, woo!
Good job! Mambo, cha-cha-cha, woo!

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:30.330
I did a good job guessing! Mambo, woo!
Cha-cha-cha, mambo, woo!

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:33.000
Hey, now, let's just
get back to the party.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:35.000
I... got nothing.

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:39.000
I didn't get a present
ready for you.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:43.670
What!? Are you really
the "empty-handed alien"!?

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:46.680
I heard about it
from Tsuyoshi-kun.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.680
He said you were
really at a loss.

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.510
I'm glad you had trouble
making up your mind,

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:53.520
so I'll let that go
as your present.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:54.680
Thanks.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:00.360
Sana-chan! This party
is turning out to be incredible!

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.440
Ooh, count me in!

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.490
Thanks.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:10.660
Knowing Sana-chan, she's sure
to be thrilled with whatever you get her.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:15.330
Anything would have been fine.
I should have bought her something.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:18.670
Is that so?
There's nothing left?

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:21.460
No, sorry to trouble you.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:28.630
"Just then, Zenjiro-san was..."

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.680
Stop taking so long to write!

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:35.350
Christmas Eve is a time
for romance, all right!

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:37.020
Merry Christmas,
Sumire.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:40.310
As if! I'd bettuh
polish my front teeth.

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:41.690
What's that?

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:44.650
That's strange.
Taiko drums at Christmas?

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:47.690
I- it seems like I've hoid them
someplace befo-uh-

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:50.200
I- it can't be...
it can't be...

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:52.990
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:59.210
Merry Christmas!!

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:07.300
--Oh, let's relive that day once more!
Return, limbo! Again, limbo!
--B- but today isn't Christmas, right?
And yet why... why? I- it can't be...

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:12.970
It can't be! You can't be
Sumire-chan, right?

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:17.980
Yes, my name is
"Andoh Polynesian Sumire!"

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:22.650
Let's limbo!
Holy night special!

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:26.980
Come! Come!
Together!

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:31.530
This isn't right!
This can't be Christmas!

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:36.120
We wish you good cheer!

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:36.200
"Zenjiro, prisoner of love"

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.330
Yum! Yum!

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:42.500
What was that?

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:46.840
Hey! It looks like you're having fun
without the main character! I'm coming, too!

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:49.670
Before you do, there's
a telephone call for you.

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:50.670
For me?

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:53.010
Yes.
From Kamura-kun.

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:55.010
Naozumi-kun?

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:58.350
Hey, Sana-chan!
How's the party?

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:02.600
I'm at Kamura Academy right now.
Everyone else is here, too.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:05.270
Yay! Sana-chan!

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:07.610
Then, Naozumi-kun,
your plans every year are-?

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:10.940
Mm-hmm. I spend Christmas Eve
at Kamura Academy.

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:15.950
After all, this is my home,
and everyone is here waiting for me.

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:20.620
Anyhow, Sana-chan, we have
a present for you from all of us.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.290
W- what?

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.960
1, 2, 3...

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:28.960
♪ Merry Christmas,
we gather here tonight, ♪

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:34.970
♪ filled with gratitude
for the Lord's guidance. ♪

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:41.310
♪ To those who are happy,
and those who are sad, ♪

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:47.310
♪ tonight we sing to you
"Merry Christmas." ♪

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:53.650
♪ Merry Christmas,
we wish your heart. ♪

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:59.660
♪ May this night be filled
with hopes and dreams, ♪

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:05.670
♪ and love for everyone
born into this world. ♪

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:11.960
♪ Tonight we wish you
a merry Christmas. ♪

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:18.970
Naozumi-kun sure is a nice guy.
Much, much nicer than I thought.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:20.970
Take this!

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:21.970
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:23.980
Sana-chan,
what were you doing?

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:27.310
I got a phone call
from Naozumi-kun.

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:29.150
From Kamura-kun!?

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:32.280
--Everyone at Kamura Academy
sang a Christmas song for me.
--Oh, he's so cool! I love-love him!
Ah, bamboo shoots and red ginger!

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.780
--He said it was his present.
--Oh, he's so cool! I love-love him!
Ah, bamboo shoots and red ginger!

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:40.160
Ah, this is unusual!
A stray dog!

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:40.830
See here!

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:44.000
Do you think it's alright to just come
into someone else's home without asking?

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:47.330
Well, I don't care, I don't care!
You must be hungry, huh?

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:49.250
Here.
It's beef jerky.

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:53.840
--Were you abandoned?
--That's dangerous, Sana-chan!
He's a stray dog!

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:55.340
You're going to get bitten!

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:57.760
Come here.
I'm nothing to be afraid of.

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:06.600
He was hungry, all right!
Come along.

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:08.940
You can come
visit me anytime!

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:12.610
I wonder if that's
all I am to her.

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:14.690
I wonder if the reason
why she cares about me

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:16.950
has nothing to do with
whether or not she likes me,

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:20.950
but instead, it's how she just can't
leave a lonesome, stray dog alone.

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:25.620
--A- Akito-kun...
you do have stray dog ears.
--These are Babbit ears.

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:27.960
How can you pop in
during a scene like this?

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:32.130
Sana-chan is a little bit-
no, make that fairly dense.

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:32.960
Yeah.

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.460
If you love her,

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:37.970
you have to clearly tell her "I love you,"
or it won't get through to her.

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:52.650
Thank you for your hospitality!

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:57.650
Together with Asako
on Christmas Eve...

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:01.660
Sana, there's still
someone out in the yard.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:06.290
Hayama...

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:08.960
What are you doing?

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:10.960
What is that thing!?

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:15.300
Well, you know... I'm not sure
what it is, but it's yours.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:17.590
What?

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:19.590
A present?

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:20.590
Thanks!

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:21.640
S- sure...

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:25.310
Woo-hoo! A present
from Hayama! Woo-hoo!

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:26.930
So, did you have fun today?

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:27.970
I guess so.

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:31.480
Really?
Good, good.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:32.770
If you love her,

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:36.650
you have to clearly tell her "I love you,"
or it won't get through to her...
through to her...

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:40.320
All right! Sana took
command of Christmas!

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:41.490
Shut up.

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:48.620
--I...
--What's wrong, sir?

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.620
Oh? Do you need
the bathroom?

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:51.290
No...

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:57.000
--Sana-chan is dense. You have to clearly
tell her, or it won't get through to her.
--A bedpan? A butt? A belly-button?
A big salamander?

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:44.010
She could have turned away
from that if she had wanted to...

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:46.720
S- Sana-chan!
My Sana-chan!

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:49.390
Is she your daughter!?

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:52.560
He did it again...

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:55.150
Somehow,
I couldn't turn away...

00:20:57.060 --> 00:21:01.990
Sometimes, Hayama's eyes
can paralyze others...

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:05.320
That first kiss
tasted like lemons.

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:08.990
That's because I dumped lemon juice
on him before it happened.

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:11.660
But today's...

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:15.670
...tasted just like his lips.

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:19.670
Was today my first kiss?
My kiss?

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:22.170
As much as I didn't want
to be kissed for that commercial,

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:25.180
I couldn't turn away today.

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:28.180
Why?
Why is that!?

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:39.560
Asako...

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:44.570
--Why am I all alone on Christmas Eve?
What's more, Sana-chan got...
--A couple! A couple! A couple of Babbits!

00:21:44.690 --> 00:21:46.700
Asako!

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.040
What's this?

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:55.040
--Well, see you next year!
--Thanks for everything!

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:57.710
I don't get it.

00:21:57.710 --> 00:22:01.380
Why?
Why?

00:22:12.970 --> 00:22:15.140
Hey! Who the hell
are you guys!?

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:21.440
What is it? What is it?
It's so early in the morning...

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:23.110
"Seized"

00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:25.320
What is this!?
What's going on!?

00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:29.990
The Kurata household...
has gone bankrupt.

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:32.660
Bankrupt!?

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:35.040
"Seized"

00:22:36.330 --> 00:22:40.540
Oops, I forgot.
This week's Sana-chan!

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:42.170
"Back against the wall."

00:22:42.670 --> 00:22:47.670
That's what you say about times like these.

00:22:48.930 --> 00:22:52.390
In dire straits,

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:55.970
I've been waiting for an answer.

00:22:56.470 --> 00:22:59.850
My confessions are worked out
long in advance,

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:04.940
to always go along with the scenario.

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:10.990
My heart may be settled, but my mind is in a...

00:23:11.240 --> 00:23:13.200
...panic!!

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:19.040
When my friends invite me by, suddenly,

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:21.750
he's there.

00:23:22.670 --> 00:23:25.000
And our usual classroom...

00:23:25.210 --> 00:23:27.590
...quick-changes into a merry-go-round...

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:30.090
...for two.

00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:33.550
Although I've said nothing but wisecracks...

00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:38.310
...up to now, just for today,

00:23:39.230 --> 00:23:41.900
I'm going to be honest and sincere,

00:23:42.100 --> 00:23:46.610
so BOY, take a look my way!

00:23:47.530 --> 00:23:52.200
When my friends invite me by, suddenly,

00:23:52.360 --> 00:23:54.870
he's there,

00:23:55.830 --> 00:23:58.040
And our usual classroom...

00:23:58.290 --> 00:24:00.620
...quick-changes into a merry-go-round...

00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:03.120
...for two.

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:09.460
Hoy! In Sana-chan's
next adventures...

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:14.300
H- h- how can we suddenly be bankrupt!?
You can't miss what happens next time, sir!

00:24:14.300 --> 00:24:16.640
Except that for some reason
the continuation of this story

00:24:16.640 --> 00:24:18.310
is being moved to the episode
after the next one.

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:20.980
Next time on Kodomo no Omocha,
Episode 39, part 1,

00:24:20.980 --> 00:24:23.310
the saga of the verminous Maya-mom's
attack on the Land of Kuraata,

00:24:23.310 --> 00:24:25.310
"100 Haya-moths and the Scales of Fury,"

00:24:25.310 --> 00:24:29.320
and part 2, "Sabin-ga-bibin-ga-bonba-bibo,"
a deluxe 2nd story thrown in as well!

00:24:29.320 --> 00:24:31.650
Yeah, take them,
you thief!

00:24:31.650 --> 00:24:34.660
Uh, what's that "babin" stuff
in the second half?
